course: dictionary
lesson: 11078
title: Many meanings of well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Well is a good example. «She sings well» means she sings in a good way. «I feel well» means she is healthy. It is the same word doing a different job.
explain: Look at the words around well. In «young Portly hasn't learnt to swim very well yet», well means in a good way, and the word yet tells you he is still learning. In «Get well soon», the words soon and get show that well means healthy again.
explain: Well can also be a noun: a deep hole in the ground where people get water or oil. Use the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Well can be an adverb, an adjective, a noun, or an interjection.
fact: As an adverb, well means in a good or right way, as in «she sings well».
fact: As an adjective, well means healthy, as in «I feel well» or «Are you well?».
fact: A well is a deep hole in the ground where people get water or oil. Wells often appear in stories, like a frog at the bottom of a well.
fact: «Well...» at the start of a sentence shows you are stopping to think. «As well» means also, and «as well as» means and also.
exercise: «LEGO is a Danish company, and its name comes from the Danish "leg godt", meaning "play well".» What does well mean in "play well"? | Also | *In a good way | Healthy and strong | A deep hole in the ground
exercise: «Well... I suppose we could try again.» What does Well... at the start of this sentence show? | The speaker means also | The speaker is in a deep hole | *The speaker is stopping to think | The speaker is healthy
exercise: The frog fell to the bottom of the old stone well. What is a well in this sentence? | *A deep hole in the ground where people get water | A fast kind of bird | A short break from work | A soft padded sofa
test: «Dinner was ready, and as well as the soup we had bread.» What does "as well as" mean here? | In a good way | *And also | Healthy again | A deep hole
test: «Get well soon», said Mum when I was ill. What does well mean? | Also | *Healthy again | A deep hole in the ground | In a good way
exam: «Oh well, we will try again tomorrow.» What does Oh well show? | *Accepting something and moving on | A deep hole in the ground | Also | Being very healthy
